.SS "\fBParticle\fP setTrail (\fBParticleTrailOptions\fP options)"

.PP
Configure a bounded ribbon following the particle's motion\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIoptions\fP Trail settings; omitted fields use \fBParticleTrailOptions\fP defaults\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The receiver for call chaining\&.
.RE
.PP
The ribbon records positions in layer coordinates after particle motion and physics\&. \fBCamera\fP motion does not add history\&. Width and minimum distance are layer units; lifetime and sampleInterval are simulation seconds\&. Width and opacity interpolate linearly toward endWidth and endOpacity as each sample ages\&. \fBColor\fP alpha multiplies the sampled particle opacity\&. A temporary head joins the latest stored point to the current position\&. maxPoints bounds stored history; reaching that limit shortens the visible trail\&. Rendering uses solid, antialiased CPU ribbons with normal alpha blending\&.

.PP
Calling setTrail again replaces the configuration and clears history\&. \fBParticle\fP emitter templates copy settings with empty history\&. Expiring particles release their physics and particle budget slot immediately; the layer retains only their fading ribbon\&. Retired ribbons are limited to the layer's particle budget and 65536 reserved history points, evicting oldest tails first when necessary\&. Removing a particle explicitly clears its history; removeAllParticles and layer disposal also clear retired tails\&. Trail configuration and recorded script arguments are portable; live trail histories are transient and omitted from layer snapshots\&.

.PP
Layer animation pauses and scene simulation clocks also govern trail aging\&. Explicit setLocation calls reset history\&. breakDistance resets it when one simulation step moves farther than its limit; use 0 to disable this safeguard\&. Use breakTrail for other discontinuities\&. No ribbon is drawn until it has two distinct points\&.

.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
GUI targets render trails\&. Headless targets still simulate and validate them\&. No \fBImage\fP, \fBDrawing\fP, collider or physics body is required\&. This call is also available on \fBAnimationScript\fP and \fBTroupe\fP recorders for \fBParticle\fP playback targets\&.
.RE
.PP
.PP
.nf
const prototype = new pdg\&.Particle()\&.setLifetime(1\&.5)
    \&.setTrail({lifetime:0\&.4, width:6, endWidth:0, color:'orange',
               minDistance:2, maxPoints:32});
layer\&.createParticleEmitter()\&.setParticleTemplate(prototype)
    \&.setLocation(200,300)\&.setRotation(\-Math\&.PI/2)
    \&.setParticleSpeed(150,200)\&.setSpread(0\&.5)
    \&.setEmissionRate(25)\&.startEmitting();
.fi
.PP
 
